00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:02:33,859 --> 00:02:35,720
<i>It's raining.</i>

2
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:36,959
<i>Really?</i>

3
00:02:36,959 --> 00:02:38,720
<i>Don't get caught in the rain.</i>

4
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:41,499
<i>Otherwise, I'll be worried.</i>

5
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:15,960
[Episode 20]
[Mayday]

6
00:03:17,399 --> 00:03:19,040
Appearance is the face of the place,

7
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:21,799
but what drives business is the selling point.

8
00:03:21,799 --> 00:03:25,679
So I'm planning
to put most of the renovation budget into

9
00:03:25,679 --> 00:03:29,399
the exterior renovation
and the sunset-view restaurant.

10
00:03:29,399 --> 00:03:33,040
But I'm on a tight budget, so for the exterior,
I can only afford a fresh coat of paint.

11
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,420
I'm thinking of setting up

12
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:37,320
the sunset-view restaurant
on the second-floor lobby and terrace.

13
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:42,720
So, the outdoor viewing spots and window seats
will become photo-worthy spots.

14
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:45,320
At that point, the number of seats
will be crucial.

15
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,959
I want it to be exclusive enough
to make people queue for it,

16
00:03:47,959 --> 00:03:51,600
but not overcrowded
to the point they're put off.

17
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,040
As for the food,

18
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:56,320
besides the complimentary breakfast,

19
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:59,000
I plan to serve brunch from 11 a.m.,
afternoon tea later,

20
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,380
and switch to a bar in the evening.
Nothing too complicated.

21
00:04:03,119 --> 00:04:05,720
However, I have three requirements.

22
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:10,860
It has to look good, taste decent,
and look really good.

23
00:04:11,670 --> 00:04:14,760
Isn't "taste decent" a bit vague?

24
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:18,879
I can't find a top-tier chef.
"Look good" is my minimum standard.

25
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:21,840
I'll find you a chef. Go on.

26
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:24,999
For the banquet hall, I'm going to rent it out

27
00:04:24,999 --> 00:04:28,400
for immersive script entertainment.

28
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:31,239
[Sunset-View Restaurant: Scope &amp; Highlights]
"Hotel of Horror," something like that.

29
00:04:31,239 --> 00:04:33,799
Then I'll save on renovation costs
and collect venue fees.

30
00:04:33,799 --> 00:04:35,080
I can even lower the fee a bit,

31
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:38,199
but they have to design it
as a two-day-one-night event.

32
00:04:38,199 --> 00:04:40,920
That way they can
charge a higher rate per guest,

33
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,799
and I get to sell rooms too.

34
00:04:42,799 --> 00:04:44,199
Win-win.

35
00:04:44,199 --> 00:04:46,439
Interesting.

36
00:04:46,439 --> 00:04:49,879
You can't rely on mere scripted entertainment
to sell rooms, can you?

37
00:04:49,879 --> 00:04:51,319
Of course not.

38
00:04:51,319 --> 00:04:53,480
I don't have the budget for room refurbishment,

39
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:56,480
but the hotel has already had
soundproofing and blackout curtains.

40
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,920
The existing setup is good enough.

41
00:04:57,920 --> 00:05:00,679
So I'm going to upgrade the sleep experience.

42
00:05:00,679 --> 00:05:01,920
New bedding.

43
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,879
Plus, most of our guests are crew members
who've been working all day.

44
00:05:04,879 --> 00:05:07,999
I'm adding foot baths and herbal soak packs.

45
00:05:07,999 --> 00:05:12,989
It's not luxury,
but guests will sleep like babies.

46
00:05:12,989 --> 00:05:17,080
Alright, that sounds a lot more interesting.

47
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:19,040
But why did you bring me to Hengshi Air?

48
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,439
To pitch a partnership.

49
00:05:20,439 --> 00:05:22,799
I have all these rooms to sell.

50
00:05:22,799 --> 00:05:29,474
Maybe he'll like my ideas enough
to throw some money in.

51
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:32,999
Come on,

52
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:34,600
Let's go.

53
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:37,080
Give Fu Ming Yu a little shock.

54
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,679
A shock? I thought you were doing Bo'ao Air?

55
00:05:39,679 --> 00:05:41,280
What do you need him for?

56
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:47,520
Experience tells me
not to put all my eggs in one basket.

57
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:49,160
Grab my bag.

58
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:52,119
Come on, Fu Ming Yu is way too shrewd
and way too cheap.

59
00:05:52,119 --> 00:05:53,719
He...

60
00:05:54,319 --> 00:05:55,679
Hurry up.

61
00:05:55,679 --> 00:05:59,720
There's no way he's investing in you!

62
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,199
I'm in.

63
00:06:01,199 --> 00:06:03,360
You're the best, my brother-in-law!

64
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:08,280
As for the rooms, I'll send you the contact
information of the person in charge later.

65
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,199
And the investment will be in my name.

66
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:13,679
It's not a huge amount,
but it should be more than enough for you.

67
00:06:13,679 --> 00:06:15,199
Oh my gosh.

68
00:06:15,199 --> 00:06:17,520
You've really surprised me today, brother.

69
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:22,160
- You've got a real investor's eye.
- Hold on.

70
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:24,559
You two are having a great time
with this "in-law" thing.

71
00:06:24,559 --> 00:06:26,480
Did you even ask Ruan if she's okay with it?

72
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:30,359
Your proposal surprised me too.
I always thought you only did photography.

73
00:06:30,359 --> 00:06:32,960
I didn't realize you had such a solid grasp
of hotel management.

74
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:36,080
See? That's why you're the best.

75
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:38,439
You are making me feel like
I don't even know you anymore.

76
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:40,999
This is unbearable. I can't listen to this!

77
00:06:40,999 --> 00:06:43,559
- You're still here?
- You're still here?

78
00:06:43,559 --> 00:06:45,480
If you're uncomfortable, the exit's that way.

79
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,140
Help yourself.

80
00:06:50,559 --> 00:06:52,160
Trying to shake me off, Fu Ming Yu?

81
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,400
That's not happening.

82
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:56,720
Come on. Stop with the vague promises.

83
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:59,640
Give me the number. How much?

84
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:01,080
Not much.

85
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:02,319
Two million.

86
00:07:02,319 --> 00:07:03,640
Two million?

87
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:06,359
- Not enough?
- No, that's plenty.

88
00:07:06,359 --> 00:07:09,740
My startup budget wasn't even two million.

89
00:07:10,559 --> 00:07:12,960
- Five.
- Why are you making a scene over five?

90
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:16,359
- Five million!
- Stop yelling.

91
00:07:16,359 --> 00:07:17,520
No way.

92
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,960
You can't out-invest me by that much.

93
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:22,400
Fine, I'll match the two million. Can I?

94
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,600
We'll see.

95
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,559
Anyway, great working with you today, brother.

96
00:07:26,559 --> 00:07:30,040
Once the contract's signed,
we'll launch the project.

97
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,679
Don't worry. No problem.

98
00:07:31,679 --> 00:07:34,600
Then we're leaving. Won't keep you.

99
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:35,640
Brother, you're the best!

100
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:37,920
Brother, you're amazing.
Brother, we've got your back!

101
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,041
- I can back you, too!
- Time to leave.

102
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:41,484
Fu Ming Yu, don't you...
Don't go back to him. I can fund you too!

103
00:07:41,484 --> 00:07:43,040
- Go!
- Why do you beat me?

104
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,600
- Bye!
- I can fund you too!

105
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:48,140
That "brother-in-law" sounds pretty good.

106
00:07:49,439 --> 00:07:50,879
What were you thinking, Zheng You An?

107
00:07:50,879 --> 00:07:54,040
You don't really think Fu Ming Yu invested
because of your proposal, do you?

108
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:58,140
He only did it because you kept calling him
"brother-in-law," and he lost his mind.

109
00:07:58,140 --> 00:08:00,048
That's quite insulting.

110
00:08:01,359 --> 00:08:05,620
But I don't care,
as long as I've got the money.

111
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:09,160
That's not what I mean.

112
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,439
Aren't we closer than you and him?

113
00:08:11,439 --> 00:08:15,160
I call him "brother-in-law"
because we're somehow relatives.

114
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:17,559
But what about us? What are we?

115
00:08:17,559 --> 00:08:20,559
- That goes without saying.
- Friends?

116
00:08:20,559 --> 00:08:24,459
Partners at best.
But I'm not sure I want to keep it.

117
00:08:25,991 --> 00:08:27,552
We are...

118
00:08:27,552 --> 00:08:30,012
- Didn't you say before...
- Regretting it now?

119
00:08:31,959 --> 00:08:36,980
Aren't you the one who decided
it wouldn't work out before we even started?

120
00:08:38,479 --> 00:08:41,319
I'm saying I'm better than Fu Ming Yu,
aren't I?

121
00:08:41,319 --> 00:08:45,539
We work together so well.
You don't need to go looking elsewhere.

122
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:48,199
You know what?

123
00:08:48,199 --> 00:08:52,520
When I first found out Fu Ming Yu liked Ruan,
I thought they had the worst odds.

124
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:57,000
The wealth gap, the social gap,
everything was stacked against them.

125
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,959
And yet they went for it anyway
without hesitation.

126
00:08:59,959 --> 00:09:02,460
And now they look perfect together.

127
00:09:03,439 --> 00:09:07,240
- Why are we talking about them?
- Fine, let's talk about you and me.

128
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:11,120
My family hasn't been doing great
the last few years,

129
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:13,400
but we're still a good match
in terms of family and wealth.

130
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:14,959
But you?

131
00:09:14,959 --> 00:09:20,000
We haven't even taken the next step,
and you've already decided we're doomed.

132
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:24,079
Every relationship has ups and downs.

133
00:09:24,079 --> 00:09:27,479
Other people face problems
and figure out how to solve them.

134
00:09:27,479 --> 00:09:30,479
As for you, you got rid of me.

135
00:09:30,479 --> 00:09:33,040
We haven't even faced a real problem.

136
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:34,920
Problems appear only in your imagination.

137
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,640
And then you feel sorry for yourself.

138
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:41,380
You've never believed in me.

139
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:45,059
Not in this hotel, not in us.

140
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:02,799
Let's go. Why are you standing there?

141
00:10:02,799 --> 00:10:04,599
It's time to make amends.
Better late than never.

142
00:10:04,599 --> 00:10:06,460
Do you understand?

143
00:10:07,679 --> 00:10:09,400
Got it.

144
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,880
- Let me carry your bag.
- Today's outfit.

145
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:14,520
- Fine. Let me hold the door for you.
- No need. It's automatic.

146
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:15,719
Then let me treat you to a meal.

147
00:10:15,719 --> 00:10:18,699
- Be quiet.
- Barbecue? Steak?

148
00:10:29,319 --> 00:10:32,040
Does he usually cook at you two's place?

149
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:34,819
I cook sometimes. Instant noodles and stuff.

150
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,059
You know my cooking.

151
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:42,439
And what do you mean by "you two's place"?
This is my place.

152
00:10:42,439 --> 00:10:44,959
Got it. Your place.

153
00:10:44,959 --> 00:10:48,280
You work for him during the day,
and he cooks for you at night.

154
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:51,500
You two have
a pretty complicated working relationship.

155
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,040
Where is Xiao Zhen?

156
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:57,839
She just called.
She's out of the airport and on her way.

157
00:10:57,839 --> 00:10:59,920
How's she been doing?

158
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:01,400
Fine, I guess.

159
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:05,740
She's been around
studying and assessments every day.

160
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:09,240
It's been over two years now.

161
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,640
She should have moved on by now.

162
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:16,360
I've been putting off this get-together
because I didn't want her to overthink things.

163
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:17,959
How should I put it?

164
00:11:17,959 --> 00:11:21,640
She looks fine.

165
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:23,814
But I recently found out

166
00:11:23,814 --> 00:11:28,319
- she's been chatting with an AI on her phone.
- AI?

167
00:11:28,319 --> 00:11:32,240
You could say she's found an AI boyfriend
as a replacement for Lu Ming.

168
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:35,179
So now she's in a purely online relationship.

169
00:11:40,346 --> 00:11:42,442
I'll get the door.

170
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:48,120
Ruan...

171
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,520
Mr. Fu?

172
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,799
Sorry, my flight was delayed.

173
00:11:52,799 --> 00:11:55,539
No worries. Come in. They're both inside.

174
00:11:57,880 --> 00:11:59,740
Look at her.

175
00:12:02,679 --> 00:12:04,400
Why are you acting so shady?

176
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:05,679
It's terrifying.

177
00:12:05,679 --> 00:12:08,400
The door is opened
and there's Mr. Fu in an apron.

178
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:10,719
Felt like I was back at work.

179
00:12:10,719 --> 00:12:15,636
Just think of him as the house-husband.

180
00:12:17,679 --> 00:12:19,279
I can't do that.

181
00:12:19,959 --> 00:12:22,920
You two are just sitting here
eating sunflower seeds and not helping?

182
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:25,479
We'd only get in the way. Why bother?

183
00:12:25,479 --> 00:12:27,240
What are you so nervous about?

184
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:30,640
He's meeting his girlfriend's friends.

185
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,479
He's the one who should be nervous.

186
00:12:32,479 --> 00:12:34,400
- True.
- Good point.

187
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:36,000
Have some seeds.

188
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:41,479
It's him!

189
00:12:41,479 --> 00:12:43,599
It's him. I like him so much.

190
00:12:43,599 --> 00:12:45,040
Really?

191
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,899
They look alike.

192
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:07,719
Come on, eat up.

193
00:13:07,719 --> 00:13:10,140
The meat's going to get tough.

194
00:13:13,319 --> 00:13:16,092
Eat. What's wrong with you two?

195
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:54,699
Thank you, Mr. Fu.

196
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:03,400
Do you want to try something else?

197
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,401
No, thanks.

198
00:14:04,401 --> 00:14:06,400
I like scallions.

199
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:08,959
Seriously, what are you doing?

200
00:14:08,959 --> 00:14:11,380
Nothing. We're eating.

201
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:18,199
Is it because I'm here?
So you're feeling awkward?

202
00:14:18,199 --> 00:14:21,400
Of course not. We're having a great time.

203
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:23,839
I'm going to dig in and eat my fill.

204
00:14:23,839 --> 00:14:25,360
You don't have to try so hard.

205
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:27,400
Eat as usual.

206
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,599
He's not Mr. Fu right now.

207
00:14:28,599 --> 00:14:30,719
He's Fu Ming Yu, my boyfriend.

208
00:14:30,719 --> 00:14:33,079
You two should be finding fault with him.

209
00:14:33,079 --> 00:14:34,360
What are you saying?

210
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:38,020
Mr. Fu is perfect.
What flaws could he possibly have?

211
00:14:38,959 --> 00:14:42,240
It's after work hours.
You don't have to say stuff like that.

212
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:44,160
And you don't have to call me Mr. Fu
after hours either.

213
00:14:44,160 --> 00:14:46,400
Okay, Mr. Fu...

214
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,319
Then what should I call you?

215
00:14:48,319 --> 00:14:51,620
Nothing really feels right.

216
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,380
What would be appropriate?

217
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:59,000
I've got a good idea.

218
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,059
How about "Brother-in-law"?

219
00:15:06,559 --> 00:15:08,179
Doesn't sound good?

220
00:15:10,199 --> 00:15:12,240
Not appropriate?

221
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,960
Too hard to say?

222
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,500
Brother-in-law.

223
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,599
"Brother-in-law."

224
00:15:34,599 --> 00:15:36,719
Don't be like that! You're so annoying.

225
00:15:36,719 --> 00:15:38,120
How can you even say that?

226
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:40,040
- "Brother-in-law"...
- Money is hard to earn, though.

227
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:43,160
Xiao Zhen is embarrassed
because she's his employee.

228
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:44,599
But what's your excuse, Xuan?

229
00:15:44,599 --> 00:15:48,040
How come you forgot
how to eat and talk at dinner?

230
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:49,520
You have no idea.

231
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:53,719
I always thought your boyfriend
was the "cold and restrained" type.

232
00:15:53,719 --> 00:15:56,880
But today I realized he has a face
that just shuts people up.

233
00:15:56,880 --> 00:16:01,280
I couldn't even sit at the same table with him,
let alone have a conversation.

234
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:03,719
Wait, shouldn't we feel bad about this?

235
00:16:03,719 --> 00:16:07,920
Mr. Fu worked so hard to make us dinner,
and we just kicked him out.

236
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:10,000
What else could I do?

237
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
With him here, you couldn't enjoy the dinner.

238
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,020
I had to pick one thing to fix.

239
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:20,880
Anyway, I'll have to make it up to him tonight.

240
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,079
Make it up to him?

241
00:16:22,079 --> 00:16:23,640
He's the "brother-in-law," after all.

242
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:25,760
Is he easy to make up with?

243
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:27,439
Not really.

244
00:16:27,439 --> 00:16:30,439
Don't be fooled by his
"cold and restrained" face in front of others.

245
00:16:30,439 --> 00:16:34,079
When we're alone, he's totally clingy.

246
00:16:34,079 --> 00:16:36,199
Clingy?

247
00:16:36,199 --> 00:16:40,479
Sounds like my gift might come in handy.

248
00:16:40,479 --> 00:16:41,760
You brought a gift?

249
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,439
You didn't tell me.

250
00:16:43,439 --> 00:16:45,360
Just some social grease.

251
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,400
What is it?

252
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,000
Wait here.

253
00:17:06,719 --> 00:17:07,959
This...

254
00:17:07,959 --> 00:17:11,719
Now the social grease has escalated into
an unexpected romance.

255
00:17:11,719 --> 00:17:15,519
So we should leave early
and not get in the way.

256
00:17:15,519 --> 00:17:17,760
- Try it on.
- Come on, try it on.

257
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:20,379
- Try it on.
- See if it fits.

258
00:17:22,199 --> 00:17:24,339
You're something else.

259
00:17:25,310 --> 00:17:26,943
Don't be too impressed.

260
00:17:26,943 --> 00:17:28,999
You didn't even tell me.

261
00:17:28,999 --> 00:17:30,640
You're too young to understand.

262
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:33,740
Anyway, I did a good deed today.

263
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:44,600
Well...

264
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:45,601
Doesn't seem right.

265
00:17:45,601 --> 00:17:50,320
That's the most superficial sexy
I've ever seen.

266
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:55,239
Are you kidding me? You're disrespecting
sexiness and mocking modesty at the same time.

267
00:17:55,239 --> 00:17:56,479
What even is this?

268
00:17:56,479 --> 00:17:57,560
Whatever.

269
00:17:57,560 --> 00:17:59,679
At least I made an effort.

270
00:17:59,679 --> 00:18:02,519
Are you shy because we're here?

271
00:18:02,519 --> 00:18:04,560
Shy? Please.

272
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:09,020
Watch. This is more than enough
to win him over.

273
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:13,059
- More than enough?
- More than enough?

274
00:18:49,679 --> 00:18:51,999
Are you angry, brother-in-law?

275
00:18:51,999 --> 00:18:53,599
Brother-in-law?

276
00:18:59,719 --> 00:19:02,199
I'd like to interview you.

277
00:19:02,199 --> 00:19:04,920
How did you even come up with that nickname?

278
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:06,679
Ruan Si Xian.

279
00:19:06,679 --> 00:19:08,779
Do you think this is funny?

280
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:11,520
It's not funny.

281
00:19:12,759 --> 00:19:14,859
But it's very cute.

282
00:19:18,969 --> 00:19:21,999
Be good, don't be mad.

283
00:19:21,999 --> 00:19:23,679
Don't be mad.

284
00:19:23,679 --> 00:19:26,160
Ruan Si Xian. I'm seriously upset right now.

285
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,479
Don't give me that smile.

286
00:19:27,479 --> 00:19:30,279
Do you know how serious this is?

287
00:19:30,279 --> 00:19:32,439
I know.

288
00:19:32,439 --> 00:19:34,759
I shouldn't have made you eat by yourself.

289
00:19:34,759 --> 00:19:35,840
Exactly.

290
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:36,999
I was showing friendliness.

291
00:19:36,999 --> 00:19:38,959
All I said was,
"Maybe I'll go upstairs to eat,"

292
00:19:38,959 --> 00:19:42,479
and you should've eased the tension,
not just pushed me out the door.

293
00:19:42,479 --> 00:19:44,220
I'm sorry.

294
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,619
That's better.

295
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:59,320
Be good. Don't be mad, okay?

296
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:00,920
I was wrong.

297
00:20:04,519 --> 00:20:06,640
What are you doing?

298
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:08,700
Come on, don't be mad.

299
00:20:10,719 --> 00:20:12,439
I knew it.

300
00:20:12,439 --> 00:20:14,519
We're just not meant for.

301
00:20:14,519 --> 00:20:16,800
Ruan Si Xian, listen to yourself.

302
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:18,360
I prepared so many things for today.

303
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:21,020
- How are we not meant for it?
- We're meant for marriage.

304
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,160
Is that so?

305
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,660
Say it again.

306
00:20:31,759 --> 00:20:33,700
Say it again.

307
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,460
He kicked me out?

308
00:21:01,999 --> 00:21:04,900
So impossible, this "brother-in-law"!

309
00:21:20,999 --> 00:21:23,059
Morning, Captain Yue.

310
00:21:29,519 --> 00:21:33,400
Today's outbound leg
should be fine weather-wise.

311
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,279
But on the return leg,

312
00:21:35,279 --> 00:21:37,840
we might run into some precipitation
around Jiang City,

313
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:39,840
so make sure we have extra fuel.

314
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:44,759
If we hit weather,
we may need to circle for a while.

315
00:21:44,759 --> 00:21:46,539
Got it?

316
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:48,400
Copy that.

317
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:52,500
If nothing else, we board in five minutes.

318
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:57,759
Come on, keep up. Hurry up and push.
I've got stuff to do later.

319
00:21:57,759 --> 00:21:58,999
Be careful. Watch it.

320
00:21:58,999 --> 00:22:02,679
- Put it in the corner over there. Thanks.
- Got it.

321
00:22:02,679 --> 00:22:04,779
Come on, keep up!

322
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:09,180
Keep up!

323
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:12,440
[Jiang City Forecast: Light Rain]

324
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:17,779
Go!

325
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:21,160
Come on, just one more round.

326
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:24,479
Do you see the sky right now?
It's about to rain.

327
00:22:24,479 --> 00:22:26,679
If it rains,
this project gets delayed another day.

328
00:22:26,679 --> 00:22:28,640
That's money flying out the window every day.

329
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:30,759
And you're playing games?
Can you be serious for once?

330
00:22:30,759 --> 00:22:34,239
My goodness. It's just a small job.
Why do you have to do all this yourself?

331
00:22:34,239 --> 00:22:36,479
If these guys aren't enough, hire a few more.

332
00:22:36,479 --> 00:22:37,999
That would cost more!

333
00:22:37,999 --> 00:22:39,999
I'm stretching every yuan as it is.

334
00:22:39,999 --> 00:22:41,479
I don't have that much budget.

335
00:22:41,479 --> 00:22:43,560
What's a few more workers going to cost?

336
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:46,600
I've already spent so much
before this hotel even opens.

337
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,360
There's a lot more spending ahead.

338
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:51,759
I offered to invest more. You said no.

339
00:22:51,759 --> 00:22:53,359
Wait...

340
00:22:55,479 --> 00:22:57,079
Go ahead and play.

341
00:22:58,759 --> 00:23:00,160
I'm done.

342
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:02,039
Come on.

343
00:23:02,039 --> 00:23:03,679
Let's get to work.

344
00:23:03,679 --> 00:23:05,900
Branches need to be trimmed.

345
00:23:19,439 --> 00:23:23,379
And hurry, get all this stuff inside
before it rains.

346
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:33,279
Tong Le!

347
00:23:33,279 --> 00:23:35,439
- What are you doing out here?
- Stop it. It's pouring.

348
00:23:35,439 --> 00:23:38,299
- Come on, get inside.
- Almost done!

349
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:42,840
- That's enough. Get in here.
- I'm coming!

350
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:44,719
You're soaked through.

351
00:23:44,719 --> 00:23:46,319
Go.

352
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:57,160
Here, dry off. You'll catch a cold.

353
00:23:57,160 --> 00:24:01,679
I used to have to work around the weather.

354
00:24:01,679 --> 00:24:06,900
Now I own a pub, and I still have to
work around the weather.

355
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:11,439
But I think it's quite nice.

356
00:24:11,439 --> 00:24:15,360
When it rains,
this place feels like an empty island.

357
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:16,840
Just you and me.

358
00:24:16,840 --> 00:24:19,640
And we've got drinks and music.

359
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:21,240
Perfect.

360
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:24,740
If I'm not making money,
how am I supposed to pay you?

361
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:29,439
I can work for free.

362
00:24:29,439 --> 00:24:31,220
Then what do you want?

363
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:36,520
Forget it.

364
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:42,520
Whatever it is,
either labor laws won't allow it or I won't.

365
00:24:57,199 --> 00:25:00,239
Wang, is the soup ready?

366
00:25:00,239 --> 00:25:02,081
Ms. Dong, let me get it for you.

367
00:25:02,081 --> 00:25:05,260
It's fine. I'll take it over.

368
00:25:11,120 --> 00:25:12,959
Ms. Dong, are you alright?

369
00:25:12,959 --> 00:25:13,999
- I'm fine.
- Did you get scalded?

370
00:25:13,999 --> 00:25:15,360
Just a bit.

371
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:17,859
I'll get you the ointment.

372
00:25:29,279 --> 00:25:30,879
<i>Captain Yue!</i>

373
00:25:30,879 --> 00:25:33,199
[Captain Yue Yang suddenly collapsed.]
<i>Peng Fei!</i>

374
00:25:33,199 --> 00:25:35,679
<i>- Secure the captain. Now.
- What?</i>

375
00:25:35,679 --> 00:25:37,819
<i>Don't freeze. Secure him.</i>

376
00:25:42,759 --> 00:25:44,439
Captain, I made the announcement.

377
00:25:44,439 --> 00:25:46,039
There's no medical personnel on board.

378
00:25:46,039 --> 00:25:48,600
<i>Can we land in this pouring rain?</i>

379
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:51,160
<i>Get in here. Help move Captain Yue out
and get him settled.</i>

380
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:52,640
<i>You handle the passengers.</i>

381
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:55,039
<i>- Leave the rest to me.</i>
- Got it.

382
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:12,760
<i>Careful.</i>

383
00:26:13,640 --> 00:26:15,539
Let me.

384
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:19,680
<i>Come on.</i>

385
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:23,080
<i>Peng Fei, take the left seat.</i>

386
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:25,039
<i>Don't panic. Do what you did in training.</i>

387
00:26:25,039 --> 00:26:26,439
<i>Help me run the checklist.</i>

388
00:26:26,439 --> 00:26:28,039
<i>Got it.</i>

389
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:31,800
Sorry for the disturbance.

390
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:34,239
- Sorry.
- We have a passenger who's feeling unwell.

391
00:26:34,239 --> 00:26:35,999
Please remain calm.

392
00:26:35,999 --> 00:26:37,039
Yue Yang.

393
00:26:37,039 --> 00:26:39,379
Can you hear me? Yue Yang!

394
00:26:40,959 --> 00:26:42,360
<i>Mayday! Mayday! Mayday!</i>

395
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:45,279
<i>Jiang City Approach, Hengshi Air 5123.
Captain incapacitated.</i>

396
00:26:45,279 --> 00:26:47,880
<i>Request weather, approach conditions,
and radar vectors.</i>

397
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:49,160
<i>Request medical assistance on arrival.</i>

398
00:26:49,160 --> 00:26:50,640
Hengshi Air 5123. Mayday received.

399
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:52,479
Runway 22 in use.

400
00:26:52,479 --> 00:26:55,080
<i>Jiang City current weather:
wind 120 degrees at 15 meters per second.</i>

401
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:56,160
<i>Gusts 18 meters per second.</i>

402
00:26:56,160 --> 00:26:58,880
<i>Wind varying between 030 and 140 degrees.</i>

403
00:26:58,880 --> 00:27:00,759
<i>Temperature 19. QNH 1002.</i>

404
00:27:00,759 --> 00:27:01,760
<i>Moderate rain showers, wet runway.</i>

405
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,320
<i>Runway condition code five-five-five.</i>

406
00:27:03,320 --> 00:27:05,199
<i>I have holding and approaching traffic
in the area.</i>

407
00:27:05,199 --> 00:27:07,099
<i>Confirm your intentions.</i>

408
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:10,239
<i>Standby, Hengshi Air 5123.</i>

409
00:27:10,239 --> 00:27:14,840
<i>This weather is exactly like
what I trained for in the simulator.</i>

410
00:27:14,840 --> 00:27:17,896
<i>And the examiner was Captain Yue too.</i>

411
00:27:17,896 --> 00:27:19,800
[Jiang City]

412
00:27:20,519 --> 00:27:23,800
Can you check
if there's any flight information?

413
00:27:23,800 --> 00:27:26,700
- The rain's insane.
- I've been checking. Nothing.

414
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:29,199
Maybe we shouldn't go today.

415
00:27:29,199 --> 00:27:31,999
The weather is terrifying.

416
00:27:31,999 --> 00:27:33,600
Thunder, rain.

417
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:36,379
People on those planes must be terrified.

418
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:01,380
[Captain Incapacitation]
[Emergency Landing in Jiang City]

419
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:05,280
[Bai Yang]

420
00:28:05,280 --> 00:28:07,840
<i>Mr. Fu? Flight 5123 has declared an emergency.</i>

421
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:09,699
<i>We've activated the emergency response plan.</i>

422
00:28:09,699 --> 00:28:11,757
[Captain Incapacitated]
[Emergency Landing in Jiang City]

423
00:28:11,757 --> 00:28:14,200
[Captain: Yue Yang]
[First Officers: Ruan Si Xian, Shan Peng Fei]

424
00:28:16,679 --> 00:28:18,560
<i>Ruan, I've run the numbers.</i>

425
00:28:18,560 --> 00:28:20,959
<i>Crosswind 29 knots, tailwind 7 knots.</i>

426
00:28:20,959 --> 00:28:23,239
<i>Landing distance, 2168 meters.</i>

427
00:28:23,239 --> 00:28:24,400
<i>But...</i>

428
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:25,999
<i>- But what?
- We'll go on autopilot without the captain.</i>

429
00:28:25,999 --> 00:28:29,360
<i>But the manual says
the crosswind limit for autoland is 15 knots.</i>

430
00:28:29,360 --> 00:28:31,400
<i>- It's exceeded.
- Forget the autopilot.</i>

431
00:28:31,400 --> 00:28:33,999
<i>The crosswind limit for hand-fly is 32 knots.</i>

432
00:28:33,999 --> 00:28:35,479
<i>We're at 29.</i>

433
00:28:35,479 --> 00:28:36,480
<i>Within limits.</i>

434
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:39,920
<i>Captain Yue needs medical attention
as soon as possible.</i>

435
00:28:39,920 --> 00:28:40,921
<i>We've already declared Mayday.</i>

436
00:28:40,921 --> 00:28:43,920
<i>- Let's get this plane down.
- Copy that.</i>

437
00:28:43,920 --> 00:28:47,160
<i>Hengshi Air 5123,
we've decided to continue the approach.</i>

438
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:51,080
<i>Hengshi Air 5123, contact approach on 125.55.</i>

439
00:28:51,080 --> 00:28:54,460
<i>Contact approach on 125.55, Hengshi Air 5123.</i>

440
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:03,240
Mr. Fu, Captain Yue Yang is not doing well.

441
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:05,959
Tower reports strong gusts
and moderate rain showers.

442
00:29:05,959 --> 00:29:10,180
They're landing on Runway 22,
but the crosswind is quite strong.

443
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:25,680
[Still mad?]

444
00:29:38,560 --> 00:29:41,320
What does "Mayday" mean?
Does it have something to do with May?

445
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:42,959
Is it related to Mayday the band?

446
00:29:42,959 --> 00:29:44,400
Mayday?

447
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:46,039
Where did you see that?

448
00:29:46,039 --> 00:29:47,740
On the news.

449
00:29:53,360 --> 00:29:55,127
[Jiang City Hit by Rare Heavy Rainstorm]
What's wrong?

450
00:30:03,039 --> 00:30:04,279
Mom.

451
00:30:04,279 --> 00:30:06,539
How's the burn?

452
00:30:07,320 --> 00:30:08,560
Let's go to the hospital
before it gets infected.

453
00:30:08,560 --> 00:30:10,360
You An, be quiet.

454
00:30:10,360 --> 00:30:14,239
<i>Hengshi Air Flight 5123 is on approach.
We will continue to follow this story</i>

455
00:30:14,239 --> 00:30:16,840
[JCTV Reports: Jiang City Weather]
<i>and bring you updates.</i>

456
00:30:16,840 --> 00:30:19,039
My phone. Where's my phone?

457
00:30:19,039 --> 00:30:21,640
- Mom, don't panic.
- Where is my phone?

458
00:30:21,640 --> 00:30:22,840
Where is my phone?

459
00:30:22,840 --> 00:30:25,800
I just had it in my hand. Where is it?

460
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:27,400
Thank you.

461
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:33,379
<i>Sorry, the phone you have dialed
is powered off.</i>

462
00:30:39,160 --> 00:30:40,640
All vehicles, follow my lead.

463
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:43,800
Stand by for rescue operations
as soon as the aircraft comes to a stop.

464
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:45,400
Repeat! All vehicles, follow my lead.

465
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:48,360
Mr. Fu, the Ground Handling Unit is on the way.

466
00:30:48,360 --> 00:30:49,759
They're here to get a handle on the situation.

467
00:30:49,759 --> 00:30:51,120
Are you going to meet them?

468
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:52,880
Leave it to Mr. Hu. I'm staying right here.

469
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:54,480
Understood.

470
00:30:59,560 --> 00:31:00,999
Wait for me in the car.

471
00:31:00,999 --> 00:31:02,759
Xiao Zhen.

472
00:31:02,759 --> 00:31:03,920
Don't worry.

473
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:06,619
Ruan is the most capable pilot I know.

474
00:31:11,239 --> 00:31:12,759
Careful.

475
00:31:12,759 --> 00:31:14,700
Careful.

476
00:31:19,679 --> 00:31:22,160
I can't see anything from here.

477
00:31:22,160 --> 00:31:23,199
Yan An.

478
00:31:23,199 --> 00:31:24,759
I can't see anything from here.

479
00:31:24,759 --> 00:31:27,560
How are we supposed to know
if her plane has landed?

480
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:29,600
Auntie Dong, don't worry. Let me go find out.

481
00:31:29,600 --> 00:31:30,640
Then I'll go with you.

482
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:32,776
No, your wound might get infected. Let him go.

483
00:31:32,776 --> 00:31:35,039
Yes, Auntie Dong, you won't be able to
get to the tarmac anyway.

484
00:31:35,039 --> 00:31:37,679
I'll go ask right now.
I'll call you the moment I have news.

485
00:31:37,679 --> 00:31:38,840
- Alright.
- I'll be back.

486
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:40,999
- Thank you.
- Bye.

487
00:31:40,999 --> 00:31:44,439
<i>Hengshi Air 5123, cleared ILS approach,
Runway 22, report established.</i>

488
00:31:44,439 --> 00:31:48,139
<i>Cleared ILS, Runway 22,
report established, Hengshi Air 5123.</i>

489
00:31:49,039 --> 00:31:52,160
<i>G/S, LOC blue, CAT III Dual, AP 1 plus 2.</i>

490
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:53,760
<i>Checked.</i>

491
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:56,719
<i>Rain seems lighter on final.</i>

492
00:31:56,719 --> 00:31:58,319
<i>Gear down.</i>

493
00:32:02,279 --> 00:32:06,080
<i>Crosswind is within limits for now, but if
it gets any stronger, it'll go over the limit.</i>

494
00:32:06,080 --> 00:32:07,980
<i>Turn on the wipers.</i>

495
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:14,819
<i>The rain is growing heavier!</i>

496
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:19,900
<i>Visual reference in sight.
Autopilot disengaged.</i>

497
00:32:25,800 --> 00:32:29,020
Mr. Fu, the wind's shifting.

498
00:32:33,679 --> 00:32:34,680
<i>CAT I.</i>

499
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:36,640
<i>- Land.
- Checked.</i>

500
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:38,120
<i>- Above 100.
- Checked.</i>

501
00:32:38,120 --> 00:32:39,719
<i>- Decision height.
- Continue.</i>

502
00:32:39,719 --> 00:32:41,859
<i>Wind's shifting a lot.</i>

503
00:32:45,640 --> 00:32:47,880
<i>Ruan, the crab angle is getting steep.</i>

504
00:32:47,880 --> 00:32:49,619
<i>Watch the crosswind.</i>

505
00:33:02,080 --> 00:33:04,279
<i>The more urgent it is, the calmer we must be.</i>

506
00:33:04,279 --> 00:33:06,640
<i>While we race against time for the patient,</i>

507
00:33:06,640 --> 00:33:12,220
<i>we are also responsible for the safety
of the other 181 passengers on board.</i>

508
00:33:24,959 --> 00:33:27,460
Stay here, Xiao Zhen.

509
00:33:30,160 --> 00:33:33,539
Check your phone.
See if Ruan has sent you anything.

510
00:33:44,759 --> 00:33:46,619
<i>100.</i>

511
00:33:51,134 --> 00:33:54,579
<i>Ruan, the wind is turbulent.</i>

512
00:33:59,199 --> 00:34:00,819
<i>50.</i>

513
00:34:02,999 --> 00:34:04,599
<i>40.</i>

514
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:07,239
<i>30.</i>

515
00:34:07,239 --> 00:34:08,839
<i>20.</i>

516
00:34:19,200 --> 00:34:20,800
<i>Throttle back.</i>

517
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:22,920
<i>Spoilers. Reverse green.</i>

518
00:34:22,920 --> 00:34:24,559
<i>- Brakes!</i>
- It landed!

519
00:34:24,559 --> 00:34:26,340
It landed!

520
00:34:29,439 --> 00:34:31,340
<i>Direction!</i>

521
00:34:43,200 --> 00:34:45,059
<i>Nose is straightened.</i>

522
00:34:46,599 --> 00:34:49,680
Hengshi Air 5123, exit at B4.

523
00:34:49,680 --> 00:34:53,259
<i>Speed too high. Unable to exit,
Hengshi Air 5123.</i>

524
00:34:53,999 --> 00:34:55,880
What's happening now?

525
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:57,479
Mr. Yan, don't worry.

526
00:34:57,479 --> 00:34:59,760
The plane is back on the centerline.

527
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:02,959
But the wind shifted suddenly,
and the speed hasn't dropped.

528
00:35:02,959 --> 00:35:05,300
Is Ruan Si Xian on that plane?

529
00:35:09,159 --> 00:35:12,374
<i>Tailwind. Ruan, tailwind increasing.</i>

530
00:35:12,374 --> 00:35:14,159
[Hengshi Air 5123
encounters increasing tailwind]

531
00:35:14,159 --> 00:35:15,479
<i>The plane isn't slowing down.</i>

532
00:35:15,479 --> 00:35:17,559
<i>At this rate, we'll run off the runway!</i>

533
00:35:17,559 --> 00:35:20,259
Hengshi Air 5123, exit at B3.

534
00:35:38,280 --> 00:35:39,760
Don't worry.

535
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:41,800
Believe in her.

536
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:42,801
I know.

537
00:35:42,801 --> 00:35:45,599
<i>Hengshi Air 5123, exit at B2.</i>

538
00:35:45,599 --> 00:35:47,259
<i>70 knots.</i>

539
00:35:50,840 --> 00:35:51,999
<i>Crosswind is decreasing.</i>

540
00:35:51,999 --> 00:35:53,720
<i>Directional control is satisfactory.</i>

541
00:35:53,720 --> 00:35:55,683
<i>We can use reverse thrust now.</i>

542
00:35:55,683 --> 00:35:57,683
[Ruan Si Xian engages reverse thrust
for the second time]

543
00:36:02,559 --> 00:36:03,880
It's at B2.

544
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,519
Why isn't it turning off the runway?

545
00:36:05,519 --> 00:36:11,200
It should've turned at B4,
but it didn't slow down in time.

546
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:13,699
- How is it now?
- Still hasn't slowed down.

547
00:36:16,079 --> 00:36:17,840
Lu Ming.

548
00:36:17,840 --> 00:36:21,200
If you're out there, if you can hear me...

549
00:36:21,200 --> 00:36:24,720
Please make the plane stop.
Please make it stop.

550
00:36:24,720 --> 00:36:27,219
Ruan has to make it.

551
00:36:34,240 --> 00:36:36,420
Ruan Si Xian, stop!

552
00:36:43,720 --> 00:36:46,699
Hengshi Air 5123, exit at B1.

553
00:36:48,439 --> 00:36:50,179
Stop.

554
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:56,619
Stop!

555
00:37:32,320 --> 00:37:34,880
<i>- Brakes set.
- Pressure in the green.</i>

556
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:35,999
That scared me to death.

557
00:37:35,999 --> 00:37:37,959
Oh, my gosh.

558
00:37:37,959 --> 00:37:40,259
My legs are like jelly.

559
00:37:43,599 --> 00:37:46,959
They're safe.

560
00:37:46,959 --> 00:37:49,920
They're safe!

561
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,959
That's great!

562
00:37:51,959 --> 00:37:53,579
That's great!

563
00:37:54,880 --> 00:37:55,920
They're safe.

564
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:57,959
Did it stop?

565
00:37:57,959 --> 00:38:00,219
Xiao Zhen, it landed.

566
00:38:00,999 --> 00:38:04,699
It landed. Ruan is down.

567
00:38:06,519 --> 00:38:08,240
Hello, You An?

568
00:38:08,240 --> 00:38:09,360
The plane has stopped.

569
00:38:09,360 --> 00:38:10,760
- How is it?
<i>- They're safe!</i>

570
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:12,380
What happened?

571
00:38:13,639 --> 00:38:14,920
Say that again.

572
00:38:14,920 --> 00:38:16,479
<i>The plane has stopped.</i>

573
00:38:16,479 --> 00:38:17,840
<i>Rest easy.</i>

574
00:38:17,840 --> 00:38:19,079
It stopped.

575
00:38:19,079 --> 00:38:20,599
- The plane has stopped.
- It stopped.

576
00:38:20,599 --> 00:38:22,659
It stopped.

577
00:38:23,639 --> 00:38:25,559
Thank goodness it stopped.

578
00:38:25,559 --> 00:38:27,039
- It's okay.
- It stopped.

579
00:38:27,039 --> 00:38:28,559
Thank goodness.

580
00:38:28,559 --> 00:38:30,259
That's great.

581
00:38:36,639 --> 00:38:38,680
- Hello?
<i>- Xuan.</i>

582
00:38:38,680 --> 00:38:41,439
It's done. She landed.

583
00:38:41,439 --> 00:38:43,400
<i>Ruan landed.</i>

584
00:38:43,400 --> 00:38:45,519
Good.

585
00:38:45,519 --> 00:38:50,139
I knew Ruan was the best.

586
00:38:56,400 --> 00:39:00,320
<i>Hengshi Air 5123, are you able to
exit at your current position?</i>

587
00:39:00,320 --> 00:39:06,300
<i>Exiting at B1, Hengshi Air 5123.</i>

588
00:39:22,959 --> 00:39:24,360
All vehicles, move out!

589
00:39:24,360 --> 00:39:25,361
Go!

590
00:39:25,361 --> 00:39:26,519
Go! Get in!

591
00:39:26,519 --> 00:39:29,860
Move! Get in the car! Hurry!

592
00:39:59,280 --> 00:40:01,159
<i>In position. Brake set.</i>

593
00:40:01,159 --> 00:40:02,840
<i>Pressure in green. Parking brake engaged.</i>

594
00:40:02,840 --> 00:40:04,460
<i>Shutdown engines.</i>

595
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:07,599
<i>Disarm doors.</i>

596
00:40:07,599 --> 00:40:09,460
Copy, Captain Ruan.

597
00:40:11,119 --> 00:40:16,300
All flight attendants,
disarm slides and perform cross-check.

598
00:40:16,920 --> 00:40:19,360
L1 disarmed. Cross-check confirmed.

599
00:40:19,360 --> 00:40:21,320
R1 disarmed. Cross-check confirmed.

600
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:22,439
Rescue team, go!

601
00:40:22,439 --> 00:40:25,119
We have a confirmed casualty! Hurry!

602
00:40:25,119 --> 00:40:26,719
Over here!

603
00:40:27,639 --> 00:40:28,640
Don't worry.

604
00:40:28,640 --> 00:40:30,360
Everything's in place on the ground.

605
00:40:30,360 --> 00:40:31,980
Good.

606
00:40:45,159 --> 00:40:46,400
Watch your step, everyone.

607
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:47,401
- Watch your step.
- Careful.

608
00:40:47,401 --> 00:40:48,559
It's slippery.

609
00:40:48,559 --> 00:40:50,400
- Watch your step.
- Easy. Go.

610
00:40:50,400 --> 00:40:51,920
Take care.

611
00:40:51,920 --> 00:40:53,519
- Be careful. Don't rush.
- Hurry!

612
00:40:53,519 --> 00:40:54,840
Watch your step. This way.

613
00:40:54,840 --> 00:40:56,320
- Be careful.
- Easy.

614
00:40:56,320 --> 00:40:57,400
- Easy.
- Watch out, wet ground.

615
00:40:57,400 --> 00:40:58,880
- Don't rush.
- Careful not to fall.

616
00:40:58,880 --> 00:41:00,760
Watch your step. It's slippery.

617
00:41:00,760 --> 00:41:02,039
Watch your step, everyone.

618
00:41:02,039 --> 00:41:03,639
- Watch your step.
- Safety first. The ground is wet.

619
00:41:03,639 --> 00:41:04,880
Be careful not to fall.

620
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:06,079
Easy.

621
00:41:06,079 --> 00:41:07,840
Okay, easy.

622
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:09,479
- Watch your step.
- This way.

623
00:41:09,479 --> 00:41:11,720
Be careful. Watch your step.

624
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:13,479
- Don't rush.
<i>- We're safe now.</i>

625
00:41:13,479 --> 00:41:14,680
Watch your step.

626
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:16,360
Easy.

627
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:18,739
Go. Hurry.

628
00:41:19,599 --> 00:41:20,800
Come over here.

629
00:41:20,800 --> 00:41:22,619
Go.

630
00:42:34,800 --> 00:42:36,460
Don't move.

631
00:42:38,079 --> 00:42:39,980
Let me hold you a little longer.

632
00:42:42,200 --> 00:42:46,340
Were you all worried?

633
00:42:50,159 --> 00:42:52,680
But you did it.

634
00:42:52,680 --> 00:42:55,059
And you did a great job.

635
00:42:55,840 --> 00:42:57,360
You know what?

636
00:42:57,360 --> 00:42:59,959
For a moment back there,

637
00:42:59,959 --> 00:43:01,980
I was really scared.

638
00:43:06,035 --> 00:43:07,720
What are you scared of?

639
00:43:07,720 --> 00:43:11,079
Boss, you should give me a raise.

640
00:43:11,079 --> 00:43:13,039
I'm already all yours.

641
00:43:13,039 --> 00:43:14,720
Is a raise necessary?

642
00:43:14,720 --> 00:43:17,039
Business is business.

643
00:43:17,039 --> 00:43:19,094
So, are you giving me a raise or not?

644
00:43:21,840 --> 00:43:23,619
Close your eyes.

